{
  "$schema": "../schemas/node.schema.json",
  "argument_order": [
    "drop_hidden",
    "drop_zero_threshold",
    "metainput",
    "operation",
    "volumetric_holdout"
  ],
  "arguments": {
    "drop_hidden": {
      "capabilities": {
        "animated": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "has_expression": false,
        "visible": true
      },
      "classification": {
        "public": true,
        "reasons": []
      },
      "default": {
        "confidence": "scanner",
        "source": "nuke.Knob.defaultValue()",
        "value": 0.0
      },
      "description": {
        "format": "plain_text",
        "source": "nuke.Knob.tooltip()",
        "text": "Drop samples that are behind other samples with alpha 1 (ie those that are entirely obscured). This knob is not enabled for holdouts since the holdouts are only used for holding out and main samples behind or inside holdout samples with alpha 1 is held out."
      },
      "id": "arg:drop_hidden",
      "knob_type": "Boolean_Knob",
      "label": "drop hidden samples",
      "name": "drop_hidden",
      "python_type": "bool",
      "python_type_source": "generator_type_map_v1",
      "raw_script": "false",
      "shape": {
        "array_size": 1,
        "dimensions": 1,
        "height": 1,
        "width": 1
      },
      "values": {
        "kind": "examples",
        "source": "generator_reference_examples",
        "values": [
          true,
          false
        ]
      }
    },
    "drop_zero_threshold": {
      "capabilities": {
        "animated": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "has_expression": false,
        "visible": true
      },
      "classification": {
        "public": true,
        "reasons": []
      },
      "default": {
        "confidence": "scanner",
        "source": "nuke.Knob.defaultValue()",
        "value": 1e-07
      },
      "description": {
        "format": "plain_text",
        "source": "nuke.Knob.tooltip()",
        "text": "Drop samples below this alpha value from within the holdout. This can help to remove incorrect samples with very small alpha values, caused by floating point inaccuracy."
      },
      "id": "arg:drop_zero_threshold",
      "knob_type": "Array_Knob",
      "label": "drop zero threshold",
      "name": "drop_zero_threshold",
      "python_type": "float",
      "python_type_source": "generator_type_map_v1",
      "raw_script": "1e-07",
      "shape": {
        "array_size": 1,
        "dimensions": 1,
        "height": 1,
        "width": 1
      },
      "values": {
        "kind": "examples",
        "source": "generator_reference_examples",
        "values": [
          1e-07,
          0.0,
          0.5,
          1.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "metainput": {
      "capabilities": {
        "animated": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "has_expression": false,
        "visible": true
      },
      "classification": {
        "public": true,
        "reasons": []
      },
      "default": {
        "confidence": "scanner",
        "raw": 0.0,
        "source": "nuke.Knob.defaultValue()",
        "value": "B"
      },
      "description": {
        "format": "plain_text",
        "source": "nuke.Knob.tooltip()",
        "text": "Output metadata from the selected input(s).  When set to 'All' and there are keys that have the same name in both inputs keys in B will override keys in A."
      },
      "id": "arg:metainput",
      "knob_type": "Enumeration_Knob",
      "label": "metadata from",
      "name": "metainput",
      "python_type": "str",
      "python_type_source": "generator_type_map_v1",
      "raw_script": "B",
      "shape": {
        "array_size": 1,
        "dimensions": 1,
        "height": 1,
        "width": 1
      },
      "values": {
        "kind": "allowed_values",
        "source": "nuke.Knob.values()",
        "values": [
          "B",
          "A",
          "All"
        ]
      }
    },
    "operation": {
      "capabilities": {
        "animated": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "has_expression": false,
        "visible": true
      },
      "classification": {
        "public": true,
        "reasons": []
      },
      "default": {
        "confidence": "scanner",
        "raw": 0.0,
        "source": "nuke.Knob.defaultValue()",
        "value": "combine"
      },
      "description": {
        "format": "plain_text",
        "source": "nuke.Knob.tooltip()",
        "text": "How to merge the inputs.<ul><li>combine - Combine the samples from the A and B inputs according to the OpenEXR specification of interpreting deep pixels. First, it de-overlaps the samples as necessary using the standard splitting volumes mechanism. At this stage, the algorithm just adds non-overlapping samples one by one and merges completely overlapping  samples. The equations for the alpha and color calculation can be found in the OpenEXR specification.\n<li>holdout - Holdout samples from the B input by the samples in the A input(s). This can be useful for removing parts of the scene either for having a different scene or optimisation to apply some operation only on some part of the scene before adding the held out samples back.\nFirst, the algorithm de-overlaps the samples as necessary using the standard splitting volumes mechanism. Then, it holds out accordingly. The default behaviour is non-volumetric holdout. Everything is held out behind the deep front of the holdout samples. This can be changed by enabling the volumetric holdout knob.\nSamples are held out according to the T(result) = T1 * T2 equation, where T is the transparency of the samples. T = 1 - alpha. The equation can also be written this way using alpha: S(i,new) = 1 - (1 - S(i)(alpha)) * (1 - S(j)(alpha))).\nNote that the holdout behaviour is currently not standardised by OpenEXR. This may change in the future for interoperability.\n<li>plus - Add (A + B) overlapping samples from the A and B input(s) good for recombining after a Holdout. First, it de-overlaps the samples as necessary using the standard splitting volumes mechanism from the OpenEXR specification of interpreting deep pixels. Then, it adds each channel of completely overlapping samples without clamping. For non-overlapping samples, it just combines them as usual.\nNote that the plus behaviour is currently not standardised by OpenEXR. This may change in the future for interoperability.</ul>"
      },
      "id": "arg:operation",
      "knob_type": "Enumeration_Knob",
      "label": "operation",
      "name": "operation",
      "python_type": "str",
      "python_type_source": "generator_type_map_v1",
      "raw_script": "combine",
      "shape": {
        "array_size": 1,
        "dimensions": 1,
        "height": 1,
        "width": 1
      },
      "values": {
        "kind": "allowed_values",
        "source": "nuke.Knob.values()",
        "values": [
          "combine",
          "holdout",
          "plus"
        ]
      }
    },
    "volumetric_holdout": {
      "capabilities": {
        "animated": false,
        "enabled": true,
        "has_expression": false,
        "visible": true
      },
      "classification": {
